      "content": "We can refine the justification by focusing on the *quality* and *predictability* of the rest periods. Argue that the consistent, predictable 12-hour cycle, when perfectly adhered to, establishes a clearer circadian rhythm for drivers compared to the variable, longer shifts of the previous system. Furthermore, detail how the shorter, more consistent drives allow for higher levels of active recovery during mandated breaks, which research suggests is more effective than extended periods of low-intensity downtime. This positions the structure itself as the safety benefit.",
